# The read on its own, which is what the queue gate runs. It says how much it
# read, because a run over an empty tasks/ and a run over a queue full of work
# are both silence otherwise, and the gate's line would say the same either way.
#
# The two tasks write owns the two ways WORKPLAN.md's format allows, so both
# reach the comparison as the same thing: a list of paths.
run check
exit 0
file tasks/README.md
	Prose, not a task. A file with no frontmatter is not one.
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-02
	owns: [crates/fetch]
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stdout
	2 tasks, no structural collision
